# Local development defaults for the parse-line worker — COMMITTED ON PURPOSE. Contains no secrets.
#
# Loaded by `npm run dev` (`tsx --env-file=.env.development`), and by nothing else: a deployed Lambda's
# environment comes from `RecipeWorkersStack`, which never reads this file. That asymmetry is the same one
# `packages/services/recipe-service/.env.development` relies on — locally you get a working sandbox with no
# setup, while a deploy that was not told these values fails rather than guessing.
#
# ⛔ THE QUEUE NAME IS NOT FREE-FORM. `npm run local:up` synthesises every CDK app at STAGE=`dev`
# (`local-sandbox/bin/adapters.ts`) and provisions each queue under the `queueName` its template declares —
# `kitchensink-recipe-parse-dev` (`RecipeWorkersStack.ts`). A hand-written name here would make this worker
# poll a queue nothing creates, which SQS reports as an empty queue rather than as an error: the worker
# would sit there looking healthy while every line stayed `pending`. `localQueueNameParity.test.ts` derives
# both sides and asserts this, and it covers this file automatically because its discovery is "every tracked
# `.env.development`" rather than a list.
RECIPE_PARSE_QUEUE_URL=http://localhost:4566/000000000000/kitchensink-recipe-parse-dev

# ⛔ REQUIRED, and it is the endpoint override that keeps a local run OFF real AWS. Without it the SDK falls
# through to the default credential chain and the regional endpoint, so a developer with a live AWS profile
# would have the local worker talking to their account.
SQS_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4566

# The local recipe database `local:up` creates and migrates. ⚠️ NOT the RDS-IAM path `src/common/db.ts`
# builds: that signs a token against a deployed instance and cannot address a container.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/kitchensink_recipes_dev

# ⚠️ `dev` is the stage `local:up` synthesises at, and the one the offline Bedrock substitute accepts. A
# deployed stage name here is a refusal at construction, never a silent switch to real inference.
STAGE=dev
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
